      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the `upsert_document.py` script that upserts a JSON document by its primary identifier using a concrete external provider, I will choose Amazon DynamoDB as the external provider. DynamoDB is a managed NoSQL database service provided by AWS, and it allows for easy upsert operations using its `PutItem` API. I will import the `boto3` library, which is the AWS SDK for Python, to interact with DynamoDB. The script will include the necessary code to connect to DynamoDB, define the table name, and perform the upsert operation. </thinking>\n",
